{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1516833-an-arabian-nights-freehold-in-a-european-city","id":1516833,"title":"An Arabian Nights freehold in a European city","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-30T16:33:27-07:00","id":1516833,"title":"An Arabian Nights freehold in a European city","content":"I'm thinking of turning my native city of Antwerp into a chronicle setting for CtD. One thing I've considered is how a significant population of people who're ethnically Middle Eastern or North African impacts Changeling society. Reading the geography section in C20 it seems Western kiths are the default in the Arab World, though they do have a culture distinct from Western Kithain. So does it make sense that those European changelings, who belonged to the previously mentioned minorities, would be a distinct part of changeling society? (Though not separate, I'd generally still see Arabian Nights style freeholds be part of the local feudal hierarchy.) I ask cause I'm not sure to what extent the culture someone was born into matters after their Chrysalis. Would religion still matter? Can one be both a changeling and a practicing Muslim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T16:59:37-07:00","id":1516838,"title":"","content":"I'm not an expert on the subject, but the fact that you're a Changeling doesn't affect your faith directly, I mean, sometimes it's almost like you're two different people, but in reality you're just two different sides of the same person. The reaction I know from most WOD creatures is that when they become something else, like one becomes a vampire or a mage, they can still keep their old faith if it was important to them before, usually in those cases it's a version adapted to the new truths he discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:03:03-07:00","id":1516840,"title":"","content":"If the problem is the cultural issue, here are some examples from the Wikia of Changelings created by the community (from what I understand):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kith_(WOD)#African_kiths\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ki...#African_kiths</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kith_(WOD)#Jinn\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kith_(WOD)#Jinn</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:14:02-07:00","id":1516841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1516833-an-arabian-nights-freehold-in-a-european-city#post1516833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of turning my native city of Antwerp into a chronicle setting for CtD. One thing I've considered is how a significant population of people who're ethnically Middle Eastern or North African impacts Changeling society. Reading the geography section in C20 it seems Western kiths are the default in the Arab World, though they do have a culture distinct from Western Kithain. So does it make sense that those European changelings, who belonged to the previously mentioned minorities, would be a distinct part of changeling society? ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question here is more practical than logical, since if there were different types of Changeling for each region of the world they would have to be more vague, so much so that they left instructions on how to create your own changeling (I don't know if in C20 or in a supplement) based on your folklore. But if you in a rush you can ignore it just use any kith that already exist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:21:04-07:00","id":1516842,"title":"","content":"Remember that <b>The Book of the Thousand Nights and the One Night </b>has been a major literary work in Europe since the start of the 18th century. Houses and theaters decorated in an &quot;Arabian&quot; style were popular in the 18th and 19th centuries. Antwerp was in a region were the Arabian Nights were at their most popular and theater/museum hybrids were a presence in popular culture. No special issues arise from having an Arabian Nights themed freehold in Antwerp. It's no odder than a classic Hollywood themed freehold in Los Angeles or a country music themed freehold in the American south.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:21:29-07:00","id":1516843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1516833-an-arabian-nights-freehold-in-a-european-city?p=1516841#post1516841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the question here is more practical than logical, since if there were different types of Changeling for each region of the world they would have to be more vague, so much so that they left instructions on how to create your own changeling (I don't know if in C20 or in a supplement) based on your folklore. But if you in a rush you can ignore it just use any kith that already exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> For me it's not the issue. Cause although there'd definitely be some Jinn, I think it makes sense that Kithain are common among the Arabian peoples as well, cause many of those kiths are based on universal archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T02:08:44-07:00","id":1516871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1516833-an-arabian-nights-freehold-in-a-european-city?p=1516843#post1516843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> For me it's not the issue. Cause although there'd definitely be some Jinn, I think it makes sense that Kithain are common among the Arabian peoples as well, cause many of those kiths are based on universal archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our campaigns the Near Dreaming is shaped by the infusion of different cultures, their dreams and even holding onto old fables/myths leading to Chimeric changes affecting whole avenues (where banality isn\u2019t strong).<br /> <br /> So Changelings in themselves are not powerful enough to shape the Near Dreaming to this extend, they can establish a Freehold in an area with high cultural Dreams.<br /> <br /> San Francisco\u2019s Chinatown for example it\u2019s Near Dreaming appears like parts of the mythic East. (Although we run the Hsien as being similar to Kithain and Nunnehi).<br /> <br /> So a 1001 Nights Freehold would work in any city with an established Middle Eastern cultural infusion and the Eshu or Jin have then used this to anchor an Arabian Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}